{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And I would sin against Elohim.</b> The sons of Noah were commanded concerning forbidden relations — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 39:9). And it is correct, except that on account of the lack of understanding of women, he set before it that the matter is a betrayal of his master who trusts in him, and afterward he said that there is in the matter also a sin against Elohim. And it is possible to interpret \"and I would sin against Elohim\" further, regarding this betrayal, that it would be a great evil for me to have in it a sin before Elohim, for His eyes are upon the faithful of the earth (Psalms 101:6) and no deceiver comes before Him, and His word is truth — only he did not mention the prohibition of forbidden relations because he spoke with her in the manner of women:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:41:58.152854369Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}